<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">4 October in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">5 events that happened on 4 October, from 610 to 1965.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/heraclius" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/heraclius.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">610 CE <span class="tih-ago">1,416 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Heraclius reaches Constantinople to overthrow Phocas</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/heraclius">Heraclius</a>, son of the exarch of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/africa">Africa</a>, arrived at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constantinople">Constantinople</a> with a fleet from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carthage">Carthage</a> and toppled the unpopular emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/phocas">Phocas</a>. His reign saw triumph over <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/persia">Persia</a> but also the loss of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/syria">Syria</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a> to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arabs">Arabs</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/sasanian-empire">Sasanian Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/heraclius">Heraclius</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carthage">Carthage</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/phocas">Phocas</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1582">1582 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">444 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Catholic Europe switches to the Gregorian calendar</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">In <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a>, Portugal and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poland">Poland</a>, Thursday 4 October 1582 was followed directly by Friday 15 October. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pope-gregory-xiii">Pope Gregory XIII</a>'s reform dropped ten days to realign the calendar with the solar year.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1830">1830 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">196 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Belgium's provisional government declares independence</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Following the September uprising in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brussels">Brussels</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/belgium">Belgium</a>'s provisional government declared independence from the United <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-the-netherlands">Kingdom of the Netherlands</a>. The great powers recognised the new state, and later guaranteed its neutrality.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-the-netherlands">Kingdom of the Netherlands</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/belgium">Belgium</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1957">1957 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">69 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Soviet Union launches Sputnik 1</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soviet-union">Soviet Union</a> placed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sputnik-1">Sputnik 1</a>, an 84-kilogram metal sphere, into orbit, the first artificial satellite. Its radio beeps, picked up worldwide, shocked the West and launched the Space Race.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soviet-union">Soviet Union</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1965">1965 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">61 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Paul VI becomes the first pope to visit the United States</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Pope Paul VI flew to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-york">New York</a> for a one-day visit, the first by a reigning pope to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a>. He appealed for peace at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-nations-general-assembly">United Nations General Assembly</a> and celebrated Mass at Yankee Stadium.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-nations">United Nations</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-york">New York</a></div></div></li></ol>
